From 2f98d9f2fb67343f23cd6c405ea31b88adf683cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:15:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: network.USBD_NCM, Ethernet over USB, through ESP-IDF's
 network stack

MICROPY_PY_NETWORK_USBD_NCM drives lwIP's raw API, which ESP-IDF allows only
from its own tcpip task, so the esp32 port gets a driver of its own: an
esp_netif with a custom I/O driver, a link-local address and ESP-IDF's DHCP
server for the computer, and no gateway. Frames the stack sends are queued to
the scheduler, where TinyUSB runs; received ones go to esp_netif_receive().
The shared pieces learn that ESP-IDF's lwipopts.h has no LWIP_MDNS_RESPONDER,
that the MAC string is upper-case hex as Windows requires, and extmod's
driver steps aside on esp32.
